-- ----- fragment: minion_isaiah_32.sql (Isaiah 32) -----
-- Chapter: Isaiah 32 — THE RIGHTEOUS KING + THE SPIRIT POURED OUT. *Behold, a king shall reign in
-- righteousness, and princes shall rule in judgment* (32:1) — the Formed Son who HAS a Father, the
-- righteous King who fills the throne. *And a man shall be as an hiding place from the wind... as the
-- shadow of a great rock in a weary land* (32:2) — the Rock, the refuge from the storm. The vision turns
-- on the desolation (32:9-14) UNTIL the great reversal: *Until the spirit be poured upon us from on high,
-- and the wilderness be a fruitful field* (32:15) — the outpoured Spirit that makes the waste fruitful and
-- writes the Torah on the heart (Ezekiel 36:26-27), the very Spirit Joel foretold and Peter named at
-- Pentecost (Joel 2:28; Acts 2:17-18). And the fruit of that Spirit-wrought righteousness is peace:
-- *And the work of righteousness shall be peace; and the effect of righteousness quietness and assurance
-- for ever* (32:17). The righteous King, the Rock-refuge, the Spirit poured, the peace that righteousness
-- yields — one chapter holding the Formed Son, the new heart, and the fruit of the covenant kept.
-- Tag: isa32   Temp view: _s303_isa32_lookup
-- Sort band: base 26775, step 3 -> threads at 26775, 26778, 26781, 26784 (4 threads)
-- Source of EVERY row: 'canon','isaiah',32,v
--
-- Isaiah 32 coverage:
--   ★ v.1 (Behold, a king shall reign in righteousness, and princes shall rule in judgment)
--        NT:     ★★ Revelation 19:11 (in righteousness he doth judge and make war) — THREAD 1
--        Extras: none warranted (the King is named forward in the canon's own prophets/Revelation)
--        Tanakh: ★★ Jeremiah 23:5 (I will raise unto David a righteous Branch, and a King shall reign and
--                prosper), ★ Isaiah 11:4-5 (with righteousness shall he judge the poor) — THREAD 1
--   v.2 (And a man shall be as an hiding place from the wind... as the shadow of a great rock in a weary land)
--        NT:     ★ 1 Corinthians 10:4 (that Rock was Messiah — lateral) — THREAD 2
--        Extras: none warranted
--        Tanakh: ★ Isaiah 25:4 (a refuge from the storm, a shadow from the heat), ★ Psalm 32:7 (Thou art
--                my hiding place; thou shalt preserve me from trouble) — THREAD 2
--   v.3-8 (the eyes of them that see shall not be dim... the vile person / the liberal) — woven into the
--        reign of THREAD 1 in prose (the righteous reign opens blind eyes and unstops the dull); no
--        separate add forced. NT: none warranted. Extras: none warranted. Tanakh: held in THREAD 1 prose.
--   v.9-14 (Rise up, ye women that are at ease... the palaces shall be forsaken) — the desolation, the
--        covenant-lawsuit waste that the Spirit-outpouring of v.15 reverses. NT/Extras/Tanakh: none
--        separate; this is the "until" that THREAD 3 answers (recorded, not skipped).
--   ★ v.15 (Until the spirit be poured upon us from on high, and the wilderness be a fruitful field)
--        NT:     ★★ Acts 2:17 (I will pour out of my Spirit upon all flesh), ★ Acts 2:18 (on my servants
--                and on my handmaidens I will pour out... of my Spirit) — THREAD 3 (Peter at Pentecost)
--        Extras: none warranted
--        Tanakh: ★★ Joel 2:28 (I will pour out my spirit upon all flesh), ★★ Ezekiel 36:26 (A new heart
--                also will I give you, and a new spirit will I put within you), ★★ Ezekiel 36:27 (I will put
--                my spirit within you, and cause you to walk in my statutes) — THREAD 3 (Spirit writes Torah)
--   v.16 (Then judgment shall dwell in the wilderness, and righteousness remain in the fruitful field) —
--        the hinge between v.15's Spirit and v.17's peace; woven into THREAD 3/THREAD 4 prose. None forced.
--   v.17 (And the work of righteousness shall be peace; and the effect of righteousness quietness and
--        assurance for ever)
--        NT:     ★ James 3:18 (the fruit of righteousness is sown in peace of them that make peace),
--                ★ Romans 14:17 (righteousness, and peace, and joy in the Ruach HaKodesh), ★ Hebrews 12:11
--                (the peaceable fruit of righteousness) — THREAD 4
--        Extras: none warranted
--        Tanakh: ★ Psalm 85:10 (righteousness and peace have kissed each other — lateral) — THREAD 4
--   v.18-20 (my people shall dwell in a peaceable habitation... Blessed are ye that sow beside all waters)
--        — the peaceable habitation is the fruit of v.17's righteousness; woven into THREAD 4 prose. None forced.
--
-- Threads (slug — target libraries):
--   1. isaiah-32-a-king-shall-reign-in-righteousness — Tanakh (Jeremiah 23, Isaiah 11) + NT (Revelation 19) [free]
--      (★★ the righteous King = the Formed Son who HAS a Father; never co-equal, never modalist)
--   2. isaiah-32-the-shadow-of-a-great-rock-in-a-weary-land — Tanakh (Isaiah 25, Psalm 32) + NT (1 Corinthians 10) [free]
--      (the Rock / refuge from the storm; that Rock was Messiah — lateral)
--   3. isaiah-32-until-the-spirit-be-poured-upon-us-from-on-high — Tanakh (Joel 2, Ezekiel 36) + NT (Acts 2) [free]
--      (★ the Spirit poured out makes the wilderness fruitful; the Spirit that writes Torah on the heart, NOT abolishing it)
--   4. isaiah-32-the-work-of-righteousness-shall-be-peace — Tanakh (Psalm 85) + NT (James 3, Romans 14, Hebrews 12) [free]
--      (righteousness yields peace; the peaceable fruit of the covenant kept)
--
-- Framing notes:
--   ★★ THE RIGHTEOUS KING (THREAD 1): *Behold, a king shall reign in righteousness, and princes shall rule
--      in judgment* (32:1). This is the Formed Son — the One who reigns, who HAS a Father. Jeremiah names
--      him the Branch raised to David: *I will raise unto David a righteous Branch, and a King shall reign
--      and prosper, and shall execute judgment and justice in the earth* (Jeremiah 23:5), *Yahuah Tsidkenu
--      (THE LORD OUR RIGHTEOUSNESS)* (23:6). Isaiah's own throne-word: *with righteousness shall he judge
--      the poor... and righteousness shall be the girdle of his loins* (Isaiah 11:4-5). And John sees him
--      ride: *in righteousness he doth judge and make war* (Revelation 19:11), *KING OF KINGS, AND LORD OF
--      LORDS* (19:16). The righteous King is Yahusha, who is Yahuah and has a Father — NOT a co-equal
--      trinitarian person, NOT a modalist mask. One King, one righteous reign.
--   THE ROCK (THREAD 2): *And a man shall be as an hiding place from the wind, and a covert from the
--      tempest; as rivers of water in a dry place, as the shadow of a great rock in a weary land* (32:2).
--      The refuge is the same throughout: *a strength to the needy in his distress, a refuge from the storm*
--      (Isaiah 25:4); *Thou art my hiding place; thou shalt preserve me from trouble* (Psalm 32:7). And
--      Paul names the Rock that gave water in the wilderness: *that Rock was Messiah (Christ)* (1 Corinthians
--      10:4) — the great Rock in the weary land is the Formed Son who shadowed and watered his people.
--   ★ THE SPIRIT POURED OUT (THREAD 3): the desolation stands *Until the spirit be poured upon us from on
--      high, and the wilderness be a fruitful field* (32:15). This is the outpouring Joel foretold: *I will
--      pour out my spirit upon all flesh* (Joel 2:28) — which Peter declares fulfilled at Pentecost: *I
--      will pour out of my Spirit upon all flesh... on my servants and on my handmaidens* (Acts 2:17-18).
--      And Ezekiel names what that Spirit DOES: *A new heart also will I give you, and a new spirit will I
--      put within you* (Ezekiel 36:26), *And I will put my spirit within you, and cause you to walk in my
--      statutes, and ye shall keep my judgments, and do them* (36:27). The Spirit poured out does not
--      abolish the Torah — it writes it on the heart so the people WALK in the statutes. The wilderness
--      made a fruitful field is the covenant people made obedient from within.
--   RIGHTEOUSNESS YIELDS PEACE (THREAD 4): *And the work of righteousness shall be peace; and the effect of
--      righteousness quietness and assurance for ever* (32:17). James says it plainly: *the fruit of
--      righteousness is sown in peace of them that make peace* (James 3:18). Paul: *the kingdom of Elohim
--      (God) is not meat and drink; but righteousness, and peace, and joy in the Ruach HaKodesh (Holy
--      Spirit)* (Romans 14:17). Hebrews names the harvest of the chastened: *afterward it yieldeth the
--      peaceable fruit of righteousness* (Hebrews 12:11). And the Psalm sings the meeting: *righteousness
--      and peace have kissed each other* (Psalm 85:10). The peace is the FRUIT of the righteousness the
--      Spirit works — never peace apart from the covenant kept.
--   EXTRAS: none warranted on this chapter — the King, the Rock, the Spirit, and the peace are all named
--      forward within the canon's own prophets, Acts, and Revelation; no extra-canonical witness forced.
--   VERSES WITH NO SEPARATE ADD: v.3-8 (the opened eyes / vile-vs-liberal — woven into the reign of THREAD
--      1), v.9-14 (the desolation — the "until" THREAD 3 answers), v.16 (judgment and righteousness in the
--      field — the hinge into THREAD 4), v.18-20 (the peaceable habitation — fruit of THREAD 4). All
--      recorded, none silently skipped.

CREATE TEMP VIEW _s303_isa32_lookup AS
SELECT e.slug AS edition_slug, b.slug AS book_slug, c.chapter_number, v.verse_number, v.id AS verse_id
  FROM verses v JOIN chapters c ON v.chapter_id=c.id JOIN books b ON c.book_id=b.id
  JOIN editions e ON b.edition_id=e.id
 WHERE e.slug IN ('canon','enoch','jubilees','jasher','apocrypha','apocrypha-charles-vol1','pseudepigrapha','adam-eve-conflict','apocalypse-of-abraham','ascension-isaiah','sonnini-acts-29');

INSERT INTO cross_references (source_verse_id, target_verse_id, source, note, tier_required)
SELECT sv.verse_id, tv.verse_id, 'manual', i.note, i.tier::content_tier
  FROM (VALUES
    -- THREAD 1 (★★): A king shall reign in righteousness — the Formed Son who HAS a Father
    ('canon','isaiah',32,1,'canon','jeremiah',23,5,'free',
      E'*Behold, the days come, saith Yahuah (LORD), that I will raise unto David a righteous Branch, and a King shall reign and prosper, and shall execute judgment and justice in the earth* (Jeremiah 23:5). The *king* who *shall reign in righteousness* (Isaiah 32:1) is the Branch raised to David — *a King shall reign and prosper, and shall execute judgment and justice* — whose very name is *Yahuah Tsidkenu (THE LORD OUR RIGHTEOUSNESS)* (Jeremiah 23:6). He is the Formed Son, who is Yahuah and HAS a Father; not a co-equal person, not a modalist mask — the righteous King himself.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',32,1,'canon','isaiah',11,4,'free',
      E'*But with righteousness shall he judge the poor, and reprove with equity for the meek of the earth: and he shall smite the earth with the rod of his mouth, and with the breath of his lips shall he slay the wicked* (Isaiah 11:4). Isaiah''s own throne-word fills out the *king* who *shall reign in righteousness* (Isaiah 32:1): the Branch out of the stem of Jesse upon whom *the spirit of Yahuah (LORD) shall rest* (11:2), who judges *with righteousness*. The reign of 32:1 is the reign of the Spirit-anointed Branch.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',32,1,'canon','revelation',19,11,'free',
      E'*And I saw heaven opened, and behold a white horse; and he that sat upon him was called Faithful and True, and in righteousness he doth judge and make war* (Revelation 19:11). The *king* who *shall reign in righteousness* (Isaiah 32:1) is the rider John beholds — *in righteousness he doth judge and make war* — whose vesture bears the name *KING OF KINGS, AND LORD OF LORDS* (19:16). The righteous reign Isaiah foresaw is the Formed Son enthroned and riding; one King, one righteous judgment.'),

    -- THREAD 2: The shadow of a great rock — the Rock, the refuge from the storm
    ('canon','isaiah',32,2,'canon','isaiah',25,4,'free',
      E'*For thou hast been a strength to the poor, a strength to the needy in his distress, a refuge from the storm, a shadow from the heat, when the blast of the terrible ones is as a storm against the wall* (Isaiah 25:4). The *man* who *shall be as an hiding place from the wind, and a covert from the tempest... as the shadow of a great rock in a weary land* (Isaiah 32:2) is the same refuge Isaiah sings elsewhere: *a refuge from the storm, a shadow from the heat*. The King who reigns is also the covert his people hide beneath.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',32,2,'canon','psalms',32,7,'free',
      E'*Thou art my hiding place; thou shalt preserve me from trouble; thou shalt compass me about with songs of deliverance. Selah* (Psalm 32:7). The *hiding place from the wind* and *covert from the tempest* (Isaiah 32:2) is the very refuge David trusts: *Thou art my hiding place; thou shalt preserve me from trouble*. The great Rock in the weary land is the One the godly hide in from the floods of great waters.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',32,2,'canon','1-corinthians',10,4,'free',
      E'*And did all drink the same spiritual drink: for they drank of that spiritual Rock that followed them: and that Rock was Messiah (Christ)* (1 Corinthians 10:4). The *shadow of a great rock in a weary land* (Isaiah 32:2) is named forward by Paul: the Rock that gave water in the wilderness *was Messiah (Christ)* — the Formed Son who shadowed and watered his people in the dry place. The great Rock in the weary land is the Messiah himself.'),

    -- THREAD 3 (★): Until the spirit be poured upon us — the Spirit poured, the new heart, Torah on the heart
    ('canon','isaiah',32,15,'canon','joel',2,28,'free',
      E'*And it shall come to pass afterward, that I will pour out my spirit upon all flesh; and your sons and your daughters shall prophesy, your old men shall dream dreams, your young men shall see visions* (Joel 2:28). The *Until the spirit be poured upon us from on high* of Isaiah 32:15 is Joel''s same promise: *I will pour out my spirit upon all flesh*. The wilderness made *a fruitful field* (32:15) is the people drenched with the outpoured Spirit of Yahuah.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',32,15,'canon','acts',2,17,'free',
      E'*And it shall come to pass in the last days, saith Elohim (God), I will pour out of my Spirit upon all flesh: and your sons and your daughters shall prophesy, and your young men shall see visions, and your old men shall dream dreams* (Acts 2:17). Peter stands at Pentecost and names the outpouring fulfilled — *I will pour out of my Spirit upon all flesh*. The *spirit... poured upon us from on high* (Isaiah 32:15) is the Spirit fallen at Shavuot, the wilderness turned fruitful field before their eyes.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',32,15,'canon','acts',2,18,'free',
      E'*And on my servants and on my handmaidens I will pour out in those days of my Spirit; and they shall prophesy* (Acts 2:18). The Spirit *poured upon us from on high* (Isaiah 32:15) falls on all flesh without distinction — *on my servants and on my handmaidens I will pour out... of my Spirit*. The barren places are made fruitful as the outpoured Spirit fills the covenant people, high and low alike.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',32,15,'canon','ezekiel',36,26,'free',
      E'*A new heart also will I give you, and a new spirit will I put within you: and I will take away the stony heart out of your flesh, and I will give you an heart of flesh* (Ezekiel 36:26). The Spirit *poured upon us from on high* (Isaiah 32:15) that makes *the wilderness... a fruitful field* is the Spirit that gives the new heart: *a new spirit will I put within you... an heart of flesh*. The fruitful field is the heart of stone made flesh.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',32,15,'canon','ezekiel',36,27,'free',
      E'*And I will put my spirit within you, and cause you to walk in my statutes, and ye shall keep my judgments, and do them* (Ezekiel 36:27). Here is what the outpoured Spirit DOES: *cause you to walk in my statutes, and ye shall keep my judgments, and do them*. The Spirit *poured upon us from on high* (Isaiah 32:15) does not abolish the Torah — it writes the Torah on the heart so the people keep it; the wilderness made fruitful is the covenant kept from within.'),

    -- THREAD 4: The work of righteousness shall be peace — the peaceable fruit of righteousness
    ('canon','isaiah',32,17,'canon','james',3,18,'free',
      E'*And the fruit of righteousness is sown in peace of them that make peace* (James 3:18). *The work of righteousness shall be peace; and the effect of righteousness quietness and assurance for ever* (Isaiah 32:17) is James''s same harvest: *the fruit of righteousness is sown in peace*. The peace is the produce of righteousness — the wisdom from above that is *first pure, then peaceable* (James 3:17) sown in the makers of peace.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',32,17,'canon','romans',14,17,'free',
      E'*For the kingdom of Elohim (God) is not meat and drink; but righteousness, and peace, and joy in the Ruach HaKodesh (Holy Spirit)* (Romans 14:17). *The work of righteousness shall be peace* (Isaiah 32:17) is the kingdom Paul describes — *righteousness, and peace, and joy in the Ruach HaKodesh* — the very fruit of the Spirit poured out in 32:15. Righteousness first, and peace its effect, in the Holy Spirit.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',32,17,'canon','psalms',85,10,'free',
      E'*Mercy and truth are met together; righteousness and peace have kissed each other* (Psalm 85:10). *The work of righteousness shall be peace* (Isaiah 32:17) is sung in the Psalm''s embrace: *righteousness and peace have kissed each other*. Where righteousness dwells, peace is its companion — quietness and assurance for ever in the land brought back from captivity.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',32,17,'canon','hebrews',12,11,'free',
      E'*Now no chastening for the present seemeth to be joyous, but grievous: nevertheless afterward it yieldeth the peaceable fruit of righteousness unto them which are exercised thereby* (Hebrews 12:11). *The effect of righteousness* is *quietness and assurance for ever* (Isaiah 32:17) — the same *peaceable fruit of righteousness* Hebrews names as the harvest of the chastened. The work of righteousness ripens into peace.')
  ) AS i(src_edition,src_slug,src_ch,src_v,tgt_edition,tgt_slug,tgt_ch,tgt_v,tier,note)
  JOIN _s303_isa32_lookup sv ON sv.edition_slug=i.src_edition AND sv.book_slug=i.src_slug AND sv.chapter_number=i.src_ch AND sv.verse_number=i.src_v
  JOIN _s303_isa32_lookup tv ON tv.edition_slug=i.tgt_edition AND tv.book_slug=i.tgt_slug AND tv.chapter_number=i.tgt_ch AND tv.verse_number=i.tgt_v
 WHERE sv.verse_id <> tv.verse_id
ON CONFLICT (source_verse_id, target_verse_id, source) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 1 (★★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-32-a-king-shall-reign-in-righteousness',
       E'A king shall reign in righteousness — the Formed Son who has a Father',
       E'The chapter opens with the King: *Behold, a king shall reign in righteousness, and princes shall rule in judgment* (Isaiah 32:1) — and his reign opens dull eyes and ready tongues: *the eyes of them that see shall not be dim, and the ears of them that hear shall hearken* (32:3). This King is the Formed Son, the One who reigns and HAS a Father. Jeremiah names him the Branch raised to David: *Behold, the days come, saith Yahuah (LORD), that I will raise unto David a righteous Branch, and a King shall reign and prosper, and shall execute judgment and justice in the earth* (Jeremiah 23:5), and his name is *Yahuah Tsidkenu (THE LORD OUR RIGHTEOUSNESS)* (23:6). Isaiah''s own throne-word fills out the reign: *with righteousness shall he judge the poor, and reprove with equity for the meek of the earth* (Isaiah 11:4), *and righteousness shall be the girdle of his loins* (11:5) — the Branch out of Jesse on whom *the spirit of Yahuah (LORD) shall rest* (11:2). And John sees him ride out to claim the reign: *And I saw heaven opened, and behold a white horse; and he that sat upon him was called Faithful and True, and in righteousness he doth judge and make war* (Revelation 19:11), bearing the name *KING OF KINGS, AND LORD OF LORDS* (19:16). The righteous King Isaiah foresaw is Yahusha — who is Yahuah and has a Father; NOT a co-equal trinitarian person, NOT a modalist collapse. One King, one righteous reign, from the Branch in Isaiah to the rider in Revelation.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'free', 26775
  FROM _s303_isa32_lookup sv, _s303_isa32_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=32 AND sv.verse_number=1
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=32 AND ev.verse_number=1
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 2
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-32-the-shadow-of-a-great-rock-in-a-weary-land',
       E'The shadow of a great rock in a weary land — the Rock, the refuge from the storm',
       E'The righteous King is also the refuge: *And a man shall be as an hiding place from the wind, and a covert from the tempest; as rivers of water in a dry place, as the shadow of a great rock in a weary land* (Isaiah 32:2). The refuge is one across the canon. Isaiah sings it again: *For thou hast been a strength to the poor, a strength to the needy in his distress, a refuge from the storm, a shadow from the heat, when the blast of the terrible ones is as a storm against the wall* (Isaiah 25:4). David trusts it: *Thou art my hiding place; thou shalt preserve me from trouble; thou shalt compass me about with songs of deliverance* (Psalm 32:7). And Paul names the Rock that gave water in the wilderness: *they drank of that spiritual Rock that followed them: and that Rock was Messiah (Christ)* (1 Corinthians 10:4). The great Rock in the weary land — the covert from the tempest, the rivers of water in the dry place — is the Formed Son himself, the Messiah who shadowed his people from the heat and gave them drink in the desert. The King who reigns is the Rock who shelters.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'free', 26778
  FROM _s303_isa32_lookup sv, _s303_isa32_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=32 AND sv.verse_number=2
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=32 AND ev.verse_number=2
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 3 (★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-32-until-the-spirit-be-poured-upon-us-from-on-high',
       E'Until the spirit be poured upon us from on high — the Spirit poured, the Torah on the heart',
       E'The desolation of the forsaken city (32:9-14) stands under one great *Until*: *Until the spirit be poured upon us from on high, and the wilderness be a fruitful field, and the fruitful field be counted for a forest* (Isaiah 32:15). The barren waste is reversed not by human striving but by the outpoured Spirit. Joel foretold the same flood: *And it shall come to pass afterward, that I will pour out my spirit upon all flesh; and your sons and your daughters shall prophesy* (Joel 2:28). Peter stands at Pentecost and declares it fulfilled: *I will pour out of my Spirit upon all flesh... And on my servants and on my handmaidens I will pour out in those days of my Spirit; and they shall prophesy* (Acts 2:17-18) — the Spirit *poured upon us from on high* fallen at Shavuot. And Ezekiel names what that Spirit DOES within the people: *A new heart also will I give you, and a new spirit will I put within you: and I will take away the stony heart out of your flesh, and I will give you an heart of flesh* (Ezekiel 36:26), *And I will put my spirit within you, and cause you to walk in my statutes, and ye shall keep my judgments, and do them* (36:27). Here is the heart of it: the outpoured Spirit does NOT abolish the Torah — it writes the Torah on the heart so the people WALK in the statutes and keep the judgments and do them. The wilderness made a fruitful field is the covenant people made obedient from within, the heart of stone turned to flesh. *Then judgment shall dwell in the wilderness, and righteousness remain in the fruitful field* (32:16).',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'free', 26781
  FROM _s303_isa32_lookup sv, _s303_isa32_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=32 AND sv.verse_number=15
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=32 AND ev.verse_number=15
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 4
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-32-the-work-of-righteousness-shall-be-peace',
       E'The work of righteousness shall be peace — the peaceable fruit of the covenant kept',
       E'Where the Spirit is poured and righteousness remains in the field, the fruit is peace: *And the work of righteousness shall be peace; and the effect of righteousness quietness and assurance for ever. And my people shall dwell in a peaceable habitation, and in sure dwellings, and in quiet resting places* (Isaiah 32:17-18). The peace is not bought apart from the covenant kept — it is the harvest of righteousness. James says it plainly: *And the fruit of righteousness is sown in peace of them that make peace* (James 3:18), the wisdom from above that is *first pure, then peaceable* (3:17). Paul names the kingdom in the same order: *the kingdom of Elohim (God) is not meat and drink; but righteousness, and peace, and joy in the Ruach HaKodesh (Holy Spirit)* (Romans 14:17) — righteousness first, peace its effect, in the very Spirit poured out in 32:15. Hebrews names it the harvest of the chastened: *afterward it yieldeth the peaceable fruit of righteousness unto them which are exercised thereby* (Hebrews 12:11). And the Psalm sings the embrace: *Mercy and truth are met together; righteousness and peace have kissed each other* (Psalm 85:10). The work of righteousness ripens into peace; quietness and assurance for ever are the fruit of the covenant kept from a Spirit-renewed heart.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'free', 26784
  FROM _s303_isa32_lookup sv, _s303_isa32_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=32 AND sv.verse_number=17
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=32 AND ev.verse_number=18
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 1 members (★★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_thread_members (thread_id, cross_reference_id, sort_order, member_note)
SELECT t.id, cr.id, 1, E'★★ *I will raise unto David a righteous Branch, and a King shall reign and prosper, and shall execute judgment and justice in the earth* (Jeremiah 23:5) — the *king* who *shall reign in righteousness* (Isaiah 32:1) is the Branch named *Yahuah Tsidkenu (THE LORD OUR RIGHTEOUSNESS)*.'
  FROM cross_reference_threads t
  JOIN _s303_isa32_lookup sv ON sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=32 AND sv.verse_number=1
